<web-app version="3.0" metadata-complete="true"
	xmlns="http://java.sun.com/xml/ns/javaee" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
	xsi:schemaLocation="http://java.sun.com/xml/ns/javaee http://java.sun.com/xml/ns/javaee/web-app_3_0.xsd">

  <display-name>rest</display-name>

  <!-- ===================================================================
       ACRESCENTADO 2026-08-27 ; FECHA O DESVIO DE 2FA PELA PORTA SEM PREFIXO.

       Este webapp responde no contexto /rest, e o log de acesso prova que e'
       usado assim: /rest/v1/social/users/root, /rest/v1/users,
       /rest/v1/glpi-integration/settings. O nginx tem um `location /` que
       encaminha tudo, entao /rest/... e' alcancavel de fora.

       Sem GenericFilter aqui, a cadeia do ExtensibleFilter nao roda ; e com
       ela nao rodam as extensoes proprias (2FA por zona, restricoes de
       transferencia). Fechar /portal/rest e deixar /rest aberto e' fechar a
       porta e deixar a janela: basta tirar o prefixo.

       RESSALVA HONESTA: com o filtro nesta cadeia, o MfaFilter do add-on
       tambem passa a ver /rest/*. Ele exclui "/portal/rest" por prefixo, e
       "/rest/..." nao casa essa exclusao. Hoje isso nao muda nada, porque
       exo.mfa.protectedGroups esta' vazio. Se um dia for preenchido, cliente
       de API que fale com /rest pode receber redirecionamento em vez de JSON.
       O certo, nesse dia, e' acrescentar "/rest" a' exclusao do add-on ; e
       nao voltar a deixar este contexto sem filtro.
       =================================================================== -->
  <filter>
    <filter-name>GenericFilter</filter-name>
    <filter-class>org.exoplatform.web.filter.GenericFilter</filter-class>
  </filter>

  <filter>
    <filter-name>SetCurrentIdentityFilter</filter-name>
    <filter-class>org.exoplatform.services.security.web.SetCurrentIdentityFilter</filter-class>
    <init-param>
      <param-name>restoreIdentity</param-name>
      <param-value>true</param-value>
    </init-param>
  </filter>
  <filter>
    <filter-name>RestEncodingFilter</filter-name>
    <filter-class>org.exoplatform.services.rest.servlet.RestEncodingFilter</filter-class>
    <init-param>
      <param-name>REQUEST_ENCODING</param-name>
      <param-value>UTF-8</param-value>
    </init-param>
  </filter>
  <filter>
    <filter-name>PortalCheckInitFilter</filter-name>
    <filter-class>org.gatein.portal.init.PortalCheckInitFilter</filter-class>
  </filter>
  <filter>
    <filter-name>LocalizationFilter</filter-name>
    <filter-class>org.exoplatform.portal.application.localization.LocalizationFilter</filter-class>
  </filter>

  <filter-mapping>
    <filter-name>PortalCheckInitFilter</filter-name>
    <url-pattern>/*</url-pattern>
  </filter-mapping>
  <filter-mapping>
    <filter-name>LocalizationFilter</filter-name>
    <url-pattern>/*</url-pattern>
  </filter-mapping>
  <filter-mapping>
    <filter-name>SetCurrentIdentityFilter</filter-name>
    <url-pattern>/*</url-pattern>
  </filter-mapping>

  <filter-mapping>
    <filter-name>RestEncodingFilter</filter-name>
    <url-pattern>/*</url-pattern>
  </filter-mapping>

  <!-- ===================================================================
       ORDEM CORRIGIDA 2026-08-31 ; O GenericFilter TEM QUE VIR DEPOIS DO
       SetCurrentIdentityFilter.

       O GenericFilter roda a cadeia do ExtensibleFilter, e os filtros dessa
       cadeia resolvem seus servicos com
       ExoContainerContext.getCurrentContainer(). Quem publica o
       PortalContainer nessa ThreadLocal e' o SetCurrentIdentityFilter
       (setCurrentContainer -> chain.doFilter -> restaura no finally).

       Com o GenericFilter mapeado primeiro, a ThreadLocal ainda estava
       vazia, getCurrentContainer() devolvia o RootContainer, e
       getComponentInstanceOfType(MatrixService.class) devolvia null:

         NullPointerException: Cannot invoke MatrixService.isServiceEnabled()
         because "matrixService" is null
           at io.meeds.chat.web.MatrixAuthJWTFilter.doFilter:58

       Como o padrao do ExtensibleFilter e' /.*, isso derrubava /rest/*
       INTEIRO com HTTP 500 (o mesmo endpoint via /portal/rest respondia 200,
       porque no portal.war o GenericFilter ja' e' o ultimo da cadeia).

       Esta ordem e' a mesma do portal.war. Nada foi removido: o
       GenericFilter continua cobrindo /rest/*, entao 2FA por zona e
       restricoes de transferencia seguem valendo aqui — e agora com a
       identidade do usuario ja' resolvida, que e' o que esses filtros
       precisam para decidir.
       =================================================================== -->
  <filter-mapping>
    <filter-name>GenericFilter</filter-name>
    <url-pattern>/*</url-pattern>
  </filter-mapping>

  <!-- ================================================================== -->
  <!--           LISTENER                                                 -->
  <!-- ================================================================== -->
  <listener>
    <listener-class>org.exoplatform.web.GenericHttpListener</listener-class>
  </listener>
  <listener>
    <listener-class>org.exoplatform.services.security.web.JAASConversationStateListener</listener-class>
  </listener>

  <servlet>
    <description>eXo - Platform REST Server</description>
    <servlet-name>RestServer</servlet-name>
    <servlet-class>org.exoplatform.services.rest.servlet.RestServlet</servlet-class>
    <load-on-startup>4</load-on-startup>
  </servlet>

  <servlet-mapping>
    <servlet-name>RestServer</servlet-name>
    <url-pattern>/private/*</url-pattern>
  </servlet-mapping>

  <servlet-mapping>
    <servlet-name>RestServer</servlet-name>
    <url-pattern>/*</url-pattern>
  </servlet-mapping>

  <security-constraint>
    <web-resource-collection>
      <web-resource-name>rest</web-resource-name>
      <url-pattern>/private/*</url-pattern>
    </web-resource-collection>
    <auth-constraint>
      <role-name>users</role-name>
    </auth-constraint>
    <user-data-constraint>
      <transport-guarantee>NONE</transport-guarantee>
    </user-data-constraint>
  </security-constraint>

  <login-config>
    <auth-method>BASIC</auth-method>
    <realm-name>gatein-domain</realm-name>
  </login-config>

  <security-role>
    <description>the user role</description>
    <role-name>users</role-name>
  </security-role>

  <absolute-ordering/>

</web-app>

